    "summary": "Answer\nThe PankBase knowledge graph identifies a large number of genes associated with type 1 diabetes (T1D; MONDO_0005147), defined as a chronic condition characterized by minimal or absent production of insulin by the pancreas. These associations are derived from two main lines of evidence: (1) predicted effector gene relationships, and (2) colocalization (COLOC) signals between GWAS loci and expression/splicing QTLs in pancreatic islet tissue. In total, 58 unique effector genes and 18 genes with colocalization signals were identified, along with 23 GWAS-associated SNPs. Key T1D candidate genes PTPN2 and BACH2 have been shown to regulate novel IFN-α-induced crosstalk between the JAK/STAT and MAPKs pathways in human beta cells [PubMed ID: 40162226]. Genetic discovery efforts have also identified T1D risk in individuals without high-risk HLA-DR3/DR4 haplotypes, with IL2RA variation contributing to diminished regulatory T cell function [PubMed ID: 39626097]. The chemokine axis XCL1/XCR1 has been found to be upregulated in T1D and to aggravate its pathogenesis [PubMed ID: 40014407]. Additionally, increased inflammation and decreased endoplasmic reticulum stress differentiate pancreatic islets from donors with pre-symptomatic stage 1 T1D [PubMed ID: 40457096]. Beta cell dysfunction has been shown to occur independently of insulitis in T1D pathogenesis [PubMed ID: 40875294].\n\nGene overview\nThe following 58 genes are predicted effector genes of type 1 diabetes in PankBase:\n\n**Immune regulation and signaling:** PTPN22 (ENSG00000134242, chr1:113,813,811–113,871,753, negative strand, GC 38.85%) — protein tyrosine phosphatase non-receptor type 22; PTPN2 (ENSG00000175354, chr18:12,785,478–12,929,643, negative strand, GC 42.19%) — protein tyrosine phosphatase non-receptor type 2; HLA-DQA1 (ENSG00000196735, chr6:32,628,179–32,647,062, positive strand, GC 40.06%) — MHC class II DQ alpha 1; HLA-DRA (ENSG00000204287, chr6:32,439,878–32,445,046, positive strand, GC 42.91%) — MHC class II DR alpha; AIRE (ENSG00000160224, chr21:44,285,838–44,298,648, positive strand, GC 63.87%) — autoimmune regulator; IRF1 (ENSG00000125347, chr5:132,440,440–132,508,719, negative strand, GC 49.64%) — interferon regulatory factor 1; IRF4 (ENSG00000137265, chr6:391,739–411,443, positive strand, GC 48.33%) — interferon regulatory factor 4"
